(Discrepancy 3 — a top-level TEXT global PRINTED from inside a function
 defined EARLIER in the file renders a raw pointer instead of the text.
 The value itself is intact: assigning it to a local first and printing
 the local is correct, and so is a comparison against the literal. Only
 the print/format path is wrong, and only for a text (a number global is
 fine). Moving the function definition below the declaration fixes it.
 LANGUAGE.md:705 says top-level variables "can be used inside functions"
 with no ordering caveat; LANGUAGE.md:3167 leans on that same promise for
 branch-declared names ("exactly like a top-level declaration" — which it
 is, defect included, so FMT-42 stands). Reached from this section via
 FMT-42, but the defect belongs to Functions / Variables, not here.
 Pro-compiler reading: the function body is analysed before the
 declaration is seen, so `label` has no known type yet and the printer
 falls through to the number path — i.e. this is a forward-reference
 ordering rule the manual never states, not a wrong answer for a
 well-formed program.
 Written as comparisons rather than raw prints because the address,
 though stable within one build, is not something to pin in a ledger.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox probe.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   top level printed the text
   the local copy printed the text
   the comparison inside the function succeeded
   the direct print inside the function did NOT print the text
)
To 'show label'.
  a text called copied is label.
  If copied is equal to "one" then, Print "the local copy printed the text". Otherwise, Print "the local copy did NOT print the text".
  If label is equal to "one" then, Print "the comparison inside the function succeeded". Otherwise, Print "the comparison inside the function FAILED".
  a text called printed is "{label}".
  If printed is equal to "one" then, Print "the direct print inside the function printed the text". Otherwise, Print "the direct print inside the function did NOT print the text".

a text called label is "one".
If label is equal to "one" then, Print "top level printed the text". Otherwise, Print "top level did NOT print the text".
'show label'.
